+  <p class="pbv-eyebrow">Feedback group · playbook version 2</p>
+  <h1>Your mission: help 30 people <span class="pb-grad">win back a healthier life</span></h1>
+  <p class="pbv-lede">For eight weeks you’ll guide 30 people, each with a real problem like bad sleep or anxiety, as they use Aurelia. If they get better, and would miss it, Aurelia works. This guide is everything you need, in plain words.</p>
+</header>
+
+<h2>The mission in one minute</h2>
+<div class="pbv-wins">
+  <div><span class="pbv-num">1</span><b>They get better</b><span>They move into the healthy range of their own questionnaire. That’s the win we’re here for.</span></div>
+  <div><span class="pbv-num">2</span><b>They keep coming back</b><span>Three or more sessions a week, without being pushed harder each week.</span></div>
+  <div><span class="pbv-num">3</span><b>They’d miss it</b><span>At least 4 in 10 would be “very disappointed” to lose Aurelia.</span></div>
+</div>
+<p class="pbv-believe"><b>What we believe:</b> people with a common wellness problem who use Aurelia three times a week, with a little daily support from you, reach the healthy range of their problem within eight weeks, and would hate to lose it.</p>
+<p class="pbv-believe pbv-soft"><b>How we’d know we’re wrong (and that’s useful too):</b> people don’t use it even with your support; or they use it and don’t change; or they change but wouldn’t miss it.</p>
+
+<h2>Your role</h2>
+<div class="pbv-roles">
+  <div><b>🧭 The guide</b><span>Aurelia makes the sessions and the chapters. You keep people listening and honest about how they feel. Tempted to give advice? Ask a question instead, and pass on what you hear.</span></div>
+  <div><b>📓 The keeper of the story</b><span>Every contact goes in the coaching log the same day. If it isn’t in the admin, nobody can learn from it.</span></div>
+  <div><b>🛟 Not the doctor</b><span>Never explain a score to a participant, never suggest stopping a treatment, never handle a crisis alone. Safety goes to the study lead the same day.</span></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2>The six teams</h2>
+<p>Each person joins one team: the goal they pick in Aurelia’s onboarding, and one short questionnaire that measures it. Recruit to these numbers.</p>
+<table>
+<thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Goal in the app</th><th>Measured with</th><th>Finish line (healthy)</th><th>A real step forward</th><th>People</th></tr></thead>
+<tbody><tr><td><b>Bad sleep → good sleep</b></td><td>Sleep better</td><td>Insomnia Severity Index (ISI), 0–28</td><td>7 or less</td><td>6 points lower</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td><b>Anxious → calm</b></td><td>Feel calmer</td><td>GAD-7, 0–21</td><td>4 or less</td><td>4 points lower</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td><b>Mental fog → clarity</b></td><td>Clear my mind</td><td>PROMIS Cognitive Function</td><td>45 or more</td><td>5 points higher</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td><b>Low energy → energy</b></td><td>More energy</td><td>PROMIS Fatigue</td><td>54 or less</td><td>5 points lower</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td><b>Distracted → focused</b></td><td>Focus</td><td>PROMIS Cognitive Function</td><td>45 or more</td><td>5 points higher</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><b>Stressed body → regulated</b></td><td>Regulate my body</td><td>Perceived Stress Scale (PSS-10), 0–40</td><td>13 or less</td><td>4 points lower</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody>
+</table>
+<p class="pbv-small">Everyone also answers WHO-5 (well-being, 0–100) every two weeks. A gain of 10 points is a real step; 28 or below means a person follows up with them. A clinical advisor confirms these lines before week 0.</p>
+
+<h2>The journey: six levels in eleven weeks</h2>
+<div class="pbv-road">
+  <span>−3 to −1<br><b>Gather</b></span><span>W0<br><b>Day one</b></span><span>W1–2<br><b>Habit</b></span><span>W3–4<br><b>Halfway</b></span><span>W5–7<br><b>Second half</b></span><span>W8–9<br><b>Finish</b></span>
+</div>
+<p class="pbv-small">Questionnaires: WHO-5 at weeks 0, 2, 4, 6 and 8; their problem questionnaire and PHQ-9 at weeks 0, 4 and 8; interviews at weeks 0, 4 and 8; a quick check-in after every session. The admin works out every “made it” line for you in <a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Experimentation → Milestones</a>.</p>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><span class="pbv-badge">Level 0</span><div><h3>Gather the team</h3><p class="pbv-when">Three weeks before week 0 · milestone M0</p></div></div>
+  <p class="pbv-quest">Find 30 people with six different problems, get their consent, and get the tools ready.</p>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Your moves</b><ul><li>Find 4–6 people for each of the six problems, from outside the team and outside anyone’s friends.</li><li>Check each person with PHQ-9 and the exclusion list. Anyone who can’t join gets pointed to support, never just dropped.</li><li>Take their consent and give each one a code name (P01–P30). Real names stay outside every tool.</li><li>Book every first call, and agree each person’s daily time (for sleep: the evening).</li></ul></div>
+    <div class="pbv-made"><b>You’ve made it when</b><ul class="pbv-ticks"><li>30 people signed up, every group filled</li><li>Ethics review and clinical advisor have said yes</li></ul></div>
+  </div>
+  <p class="pbv-stuck"><b>Stuck?</b> Don’t start with fewer than 24. Recruit one more week rather than start a group with one person.</p>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><span class="pbv-badge">Level 1</span><div><h3>Day one</h3><p class="pbv-when">Week 0 · milestone M1</p></div></div>
+  <p class="pbv-quest">Measure everyone before they start, and get them listening within two days.</p>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Your moves</b><ul><li>Collect WHO-5, their problem questionnaire and PHQ-9 before the first session. A “before” taken after is not a before.</li><li>First interview (30 minutes): what the problem feels like, what they’ve tried, what “solved” would mean to them.</li><li>Sit with each person for their first session: onboarding, their first sentence, the first play.</li><li>Write their goal sentence in the coaching log. It’s what you’ll cheer them towards for eight weeks.</li></ul></div>
+    <div class="pbv-made"><b>You’ve made it when</b><ul class="pbv-ticks"><li>Everyone has a “before” score (100%)</li><li>9 in 10 played a first session in week 1</li></ul></div>
+  </div>
+  <p class="pbv-stuck"><b>Stuck?</b> Anyone without a “before” score doesn’t count for results. Get it before they play again.</p>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><span class="pbv-badge">Level 2</span><div><h3>Build the habit</h3><p class="pbv-when">Weeks 1–2 · milestone M2</p></div></div>
+  <p class="pbv-quest">A daily rhythm: three or more sessions a week, a quick check-in after each.</p>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Your moves</b><ul><li>One short message a day, at each person’s time. Ask, don’t lecture.</li><li>Fewer than two sessions in a week? Call them: what got in the way, and one small change (shorter, earlier, another voice).</li><li>Write every contact in their coaching log, the same day.</li><li>Send WHO-5 at the end of week 2.</li></ul></div>
+    <div class="pbv-made"><b>You’ve made it when</b><ul class="pbv-ticks"><li>7 in 10 did 3+ sessions in both weeks</li><li>WHO-5 answered by 85% or more</li></ul></div>
+  </div>
+  <p class="pbv-stuck"><b>Stuck?</b> Below 7 in 10, we’re measuring who had time, not whether Aurelia helps. Fix what’s in the way before week 3.</p>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><span class="pbv-badge">Level 3</span><div><h3>Halfway check</h3><p class="pbv-when">Weeks 3–4 · milestone M3</p></div></div>
+  <p class="pbv-quest">See what’s working, and make one improvement for the second half.</p>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Your moves</b><ul><li>Week 4: WHO-5, their problem questionnaire, PHQ-9 and the second interview, with everyone.</li><li>Bring the three biggest findings to the product team, each with who it affects and their own words.</li><li>When the change ships, tell everyone in one message: what changed and why.</li></ul></div>
+    <div class="pbv-made"><b>You’ve made it when</b><ul class="pbv-ticks"><li>85% still in</li><li>85% of due questionnaires collected</li><li>The improvement has reached the group</li></ul></div>
+  </div>
+  <p class="pbv-stuck"><b>Stuck?</b> A disappointing week 4 isn’t a verdict. It’s exactly what the improvement is for.</p>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><span class="pbv-badge">Level 4</span><div><h3>The second half</h3><p class="pbv-when">Weeks 5–7 · milestone M4</p></div></div>
+  <p class="pbv-quest">Check whether the improvement helped, and adjust once more if it didn’t.</p>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Your moves</b><ul><li>Keep the daily rhythm. People who are winning need less; people who are stuck need a call a week.</li><li>Send WHO-5 at week 6.</li><li>Follow up every safety alert the same day, and write down what you did.</li></ul></div>
+    <div class="pbv-made"><b>You’ve made it when</b><ul class="pbv-ticks"><li>6 in 10 stay regular (3+ sessions in 60% of weeks)</li><li>Every safety alert handled the same day</li></ul></div>
+  </div>
+  <p class="pbv-stuck"><b>Stuck?</b> If people drift off in the second half, ask them why on a call before changing anything else.</p>
+</section>
+<section class="pbv-level">
+  <div class="pbv-level-head"><span class="pbv-badge">Level 5</span><div><h3>The finish line</h3><p class="pbv-when">Weeks 8–9 · milestone M5</p></div></div>
+  <p class="pbv-quest">The final read, and the big decision: go, try again, or rethink.</p>
+  <div class="pbv-level-grid">
+    <div><b>Your moves</b><ul><li>Week 8: WHO-5, their problem questionnaire, PHQ-9, “would you miss it?” and the third interview.</li><li>Write one story per group: where the person started and what changed, in their words, with their consent.</li><li>Present the result in week 9 against the finish lines set before week 0.</li></ul></div>
+    <div class="pbv-made"><b>You’ve made it when</b><ul class="pbv-ticks"><li>Half gain 10+ WHO-5 points</li><li>4 in 10 reach a real improvement in their own problem</li><li>7 in 10 still in</li><li>85% of data collected</li><li>4 in 10 would be “very disappointed” to lose Aurelia</li></ul></div>
+  </div>
+  <p class="pbv-stuck"><b>Stuck?</b> The finish lines were set before week 0. Moving them after seeing the data turns a study into a story.</p>
+</section>
+
+<h2>A day in your shoes</h2>
+<div class="pbv-day">
+  <div><b>08:30</b><span>Open <a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">This week</a>: calls first, then anyone you haven’t reached in two days, then missing questionnaires.</span></div>
+  <div><b>09:00–11:00</b><span>Calls and follow-ups. Safety alerts always come first.</span></div>
+  <div><b>Their time</b><span>One short message about their own goal (below).</span></div>
+  <div><b>Same day</b><span>Log it on their page: what they said, how they feel (1–5), the next step.</span></div>
+  <div><b>16:30</b><span>Five-minute look at Wins and Engagement: who moved, who went quiet.</span></div>
+</div>
+<h3>Your week</h3>
+<ul class="pbv-ticks">
+  <li><b>Monday:</b> which level is next, and is it on track?</li>
+  <li><b>Wednesday:</b> call everyone who did fewer than two sessions last week.</li>
+  <li><b>Friday:</b> 30 minutes with the product team, the three biggest findings and who they affect.</li>
+  <li><b>Every other week:</b> WHO-5 goes out; chase it within 48 hours.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3>The daily message</h3>
+<div class="pbv-msgs"><div><b>Bad sleep</b><span>“Morning! How did last night go: roughly how long to fall asleep, and did you wake up?”</span></div><div><b>Anxious</b><span>“How is your day feeling, 1 to 5? Did the session before your meeting help, or not really?”</span></div><div><b>Mental fog</b><span>“Did you get a clear hour today? What did you play before it?”</span></div><div><b>Low energy</b><span>“How was your energy this afternoon compared with yesterday?”</span></div><div><b>Distracted</b><span>“How long did your longest focused stretch last today?”</span></div><div><b>Stressed body</b><span>“Where do you feel it today? Did the breathing chapter change anything?”</span></div></div>
+<p class="pbv-small">One question, about their own goal, at the time they chose. Never “did you do your session?”.</p>
+<h3>When someone drifts away</h3>
+<table><thead><tr><th>What happens</th><th>What you do</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td>Missed a day</td><td>Your usual message. No comment on the miss.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Not reached for 2 days</td><td>A second message, then a short call.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Fewer than 2 sessions in a week</td><td>A call: what got in the way, and one small change.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Two questionnaires missed</td><td>A call, and offer to fill it in together.</td></tr>
+<tr><td><b>Any sign of crisis or harm</b></td><td><b>Stop coaching. Crisis resources now, and the study lead the same day. Never alone.</b></td></tr>
+</tbody></table>
+
+<h2>Making Aurelia better, together</h2>
+<p>The study isn’t only a test. It’s how Aurelia gets better while people use it. One loop, every week:</p>
+<div class="pbv-loop"><span><b>Listen</b> coaching log, interviews, check-ins</span><span><b>Pick</b> how many it hits × how much it stops them</span><span><b>Change</b> one change, on staging first</span><span><b>Tell</b> participants what changed and why</span><span><b>Check</b> same measures, before and after</span></div>
+<ul class="pbv-ticks">
+  <li>At most one big change in each half (halfway, then once more if needed).</li>
+  <li>The questionnaires and their timing never change.</li>
+  <li>Every change is written down with the date it reached the group.</li>
+</ul>
+<p class="pbv-example"><b>A great finding sounds like:</b> “Four of six in the sleep team stop the session halfway because the voice is too fast (P02, P04, P05, P06; coaching log 3–5 Nov).” Who, how many, their words, where it’s written.</p>
+
+<h2>Your dashboard</h2>
+<p>Everything lives in <a href="/admin/experimentation">admin → Experimentation</a>. If a question isn’t answered there, tell the product team: that’s a gap in the tool, not a reason for a spreadsheet.</p>
+<table><thead><tr><th>Your question</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td>Which level are we on, and is it on track?</td><td><a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Milestones</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td>What do I do today?</td><td><a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">This week</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td>Who has won?</td><td><a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Wins</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td>Is using it going with getting better?</td><td><a href="/admin/experimentation/v2">Engagement</a></td></tr>
+<tr><td>How is this one person doing?</td><td><a href="/admin/experimentation/P01">Their page</a>: measures, sessions, coaching log</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Is any data missing?</td><td><a href="/admin/experimentation">Data &amp; safety</a></td></tr>
+</tbody></table>
+<p class="pbv-small">Today the admin shows sample data made by the same rules the real data will use, and the coaching log saves in your browser until the backend exists.</p>
+
+<h2>The promises we always keep</h2>
+<div class="pbv-promises">
+  <div><b>Privacy</b><ul><li>Code names (P01–P30) everywhere; real names stay outside every tool.</li><li>No names or contact details in the coaching log.</li><li>Journal and wearable data only with their own consent.</li></ul></div>
+  <div><b>Safety</b><ul><li>PHQ-9 item 9 above zero, WHO-5 of 28 or below, or any report of harm: the study lead calls the same day.</li><li>Crisis resources first, always.</li><li>Aurelia is not a treatment and never replaces one.</li></ul></div>
+  <div><b>Honesty</b><ul><li>Finish lines are fixed before week 0.</li><li>People who leave stay in the count.</li><li>We never claim Aurelia caused a change: there is no control group.</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2>Week 9: the big moment</h2>
+<div class="pbv-decide">
+  <div class="go"><b>Go 🚀</b><span>Most finish lines met, including “their own problem improves” and “would miss it”. Plan a proper trial and open a wider beta for the teams that won.</span></div>
+  <div class="again"><b>Try again 🔁</b><span>People use it and stay, but results fall short. Another eight weeks on the same design, with the changes the data points to.</span></div>
+  <div class="rethink"><b>Rethink 🧭</b><span>People don’t use it even with daily support, or wouldn’t miss it. Stop and rethink the core before building more.</span></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2>Ready for week 0?</h2>
+<ul class="pbv-check">
+  <li>The plan, the finish lines and this playbook approved <em>Product and business owners</em></li>
+  <li>Clinical advisor, ethics review, questionnaire licences (ISI, PSS-10) <em>Product owner</em></li>
+  <li>Accounts that stay signed in; study sign-up and consent in the app <em>Product team</em></li>
+  <li>Questionnaire screens with reminders; the safety alert to the study lead <em>Product team</em></li>
+  <li>The admin on real data, including the coaching log <em>Product team</em></li>
+  <li>30 people recruited, checked and consented; first calls booked <em>You</em></li>
+</ul>
+
+<div class="pbv-send">
+  <b>Thirty people. Eight weeks. One question: does Aurelia help?</b>
+  <span>You’re the person who finds out. Go win it for them.</span>
+</div>
+<p class="pbv-small">The full study protocol (measures, data, safety, analysis) is the appendix of <b>Version 1</b> of this playbook.</p>
+</div>
